---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <SectionHeader
      title="About Me"
      subtitle="My journey, philosophy, and how I approach engineering problems."
    />

    <div class="space-y-12 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
      {/* Background */}
      <section>
        <h3 class="mb-4 text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">Background</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          I have spent the last 8 years building software for companies ranging
          from early-stage startups to established enterprises. My journey began
          in pure mathematics, which instilled in me a love for logic and
          structure. This foundation naturally evolved into a career in software
          engineering, where I apply rigorous thinking to build systems that are
          not just functional, but reliable and maintainable.
        </p>
        <p>
          Currently, I focus on the intersection of scalable frontend
          architectures and developer experience. I believe that the quality of
          the internal codebase is directly reflected in the quality of the user
          experience.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* Philosophy */}
      <section>
        <h3 class="mb-4 text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">
          Engineering Philosophy
        </h3>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="min-w-[120px] font-semibold text-gray-900"
              >Simplicity</span
            >
            <span
              >I prefer boring, proven solutions over hype. Complexity should
              only be introduced when absolutely necessary.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="min-w-[120px] font-semibold text-gray-900"
              >Clarity</span
            >
            <span
              >Code is read much more often than it is written. I write code
              that my teammates (and future self) can understand without
              ambiguity.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="min-w-[120px] font-semibold text-gray-900"
              >User-Centric</span
            >
            <span
              >Technology is a tool to solve human problems. Technical decisions
              must always align with the value delivered to the end user.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* Current Focus */}
      <section>
        <h3 class="mb-4 text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">Current Focus</h3>
        <p>
          Lately, I've been diving deep into <strong>Rust</strong> for system-level
          tooling and exploring <strong>Agentic AI workflows</strong> to automate
          repetitive development tasks.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* Contact */}
      <section class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
        <h3 class="mb-6 text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">Get in Touch</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <a
            href="https://github.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="flex items-center gap-3 border border-gray-200 p-4 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-50"
          >
            <Icon name="mdi:github" class="h-5 w-5 text-gray-500" />
            <span class="text-sm font-medium">github.com/johndoe</span>
          </a>
          <div
            class="flex cursor-default items-center gap-3 border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-4 text-gray-400"
          >
            <Icon name="mdi:map-marker" class="h-5 w-5" />
            <span class="text-sm font-medium">Tokyo, Japan</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
